  "preamble": "Loss of nasality and fronting of the velar nasal [ŋ] to the palatal glide [j] before front vowels and the palatal medial. In Cantonese the Middle Chinese 疑 (ŋ-) initial became j- before i and the medial -j-, while Hakka keeps ŋ- (ngi, ngien) and Mandarin has a zero initial (yí, yán).",
